## 4. Semantic pass

Read the English and the Spanish namespace by namespace against the sidecar roles. Judged
accuracy, idiom, register, glossary consistency, placeholder/ICU integrity, plurals, width.
The findings and their reasoning are in `record.json` (structured) and `report.md` (prose).

- The sidecar's operative instruction is "Preserve current login copy and casing", and the Spanish
  does: all four values are lowercase, the brand keeps its lowercase form, and the em dash in the
  page title keeps its spacing.
- Because a user types a password on this screen, the security question was asked explicitly of
  each value: none names a recipient, destination, server, endpoint or storage for the secret. The
  failure string reports only that the secret does not match. No unexpected-transmission
  implication, in either direction (no unnecessary reassurance either, which would be its own
  defect on an auth screen).
- 'iniciar sesión' is the same rendering in the page title and on the button — one action, one phrase.
- 'Wrong password.' -> 'Contraseña incorrecta.' keeps the terse sentence form and the full stop;
  there is no exclamation mark, per the style guide.
- Width: submit.label 7->14 cells (+100%) is percentage inflation on a two-word standard Spanish UI
  form; 'Entrar' would be shorter but changes register, so no change is proposed. Page title 24->31
  is in band. No maxCells declared.

